---
/* The pointer used inside product clips.

   Appearance only. Every clip owns its own path and its own click ring, drawn
   on the positioned wrapper it sits in — a shared cursor that also carried its
   choreography would have to know about every graphic it appears in.

   Drawn rather than imaged: it has to stay crisp at whatever size the graphic
   renders at, and it has to pick up the drop shadow that separates it from a
   white card underneath. */
---

<svg class="cur" viewBox="0 0 14 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
  <path
    d="M1.2 1.1 12.4 11.6H6.9l-1.6.2-.4 1.5-1.7 5.4Z"
    fill="var(--white)"
    stroke="var(--neutral-100)"
    stroke-width="1.3"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
  />
</svg>

<style>
  .cur {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 4.6cqw;
    block-size: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 2px rgb(from var(--neutral-100) r g b / 0.28));
  }
</style>
